; =============================================================================
;  08c_BarcodeSection.tdl   -   OPTIONAL, NOT IN THE DEFAULT BUNDLE
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  This file holds PATH B of 08a_BarcodeTally.tdl: the native TDL `Barcode:`
;  section that renders true Code 128 bars with no font installed.
;
;  WHY IT IS A SEPARATE FILE
;    The `Barcode:` section syntax could not be verified against official
;    documentation, and it is the one construct in JadePro most likely to be
;    rejected by a given Tally build. TDL parses an ENTIRE function before it
;    runs any of it, so an invalid `Barcode:` section does not merely disable
;    barcodes - it stops the whole JadePro.tdl from loading at all.
;
;    Earlier versions of 08a carried these sections inline and claimed that
;    setting JpUseTdlBarcode to 0 made them "inert". That was wrong: the
;    constant only chooses a rendering path at run time, it has no effect on
;    parsing. Keeping the section here means the default load is safe and the
;    capability is still one file away.
;
;  HOW TO ENABLE IT
;    1. Load 08_Core.tdl first, then 08_Barcode.tdl, then 08a, then this file.
;       (Or add it to the ORDER array in 00_Build/build.sh and rebuild.)
;    2. Set  Constant: JpUseTdlBarcode : 1  in 08a_BarcodeTally.tdl.
;    3. Reload. If Tally reports an error against this file, remove it again
;       and set JpUseTdlBarcode back to 0 - PATH A (the Code 128 font) keeps
;       printing scannable bars with no other change.
;
;  PATH A vs PATH B
;    A (default)  draws the barcode with a Code 128 FONT. Needs that font
;                 installed and selected in the print style.
;    B (this file) uses the TDL Barcode: object. No font needed, but depends
;                 on your Tally build accepting the section.
; =============================================================================

[Barcode: JpJewelCode128]
    Title: <1000, "Jewellery Barcode">
    Bar-Code: <JpJewelCode128Obj>
    Height: 30
    Rows: 1
    Columns: 1
    Width: 2

[Barcode: JpJewelCode128Obj]
    Title: <1000, "Code 128">
    Bar-Code: Code128
    Height: 30